<title>HONG KONG: East China drought impact on wheat uncertain - trade.</title>
<headline>East China drought impact on wheat uncertain - trade.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong and China traders said it was too early to assess the impact of drought reported at the weekend in China's eastern province of Shandong.</p>
<p>&quot;It's too early to tell how the winter wheat crop will be affected (by weather),&quot; said a senior Chinese trader.</p>
<p>Drought could certainly affect growth of winter wheat, but the critical months for the crop were March and April, he said.</p>
<p>Winter wheat in Shandong was harvested around June, the source said.</p>
<p>New crop corn had not yet been planted in Shandong, the source said.</p>
<p>According to a Chinese newspaper report seen in Beijing on Sunday, prolonged drought in Shandong had affected 1.6 million hectares, or 40 percent of the area planted with wheat in the province,</p>
<p>The Dazhong Daily report did not give any further details.</p>
<p>-- Mishi Saran (852) 2843 6358</p>
</text>
